# Zintl's generated JSON schemas.
#
# Nobody edits these — they exist so a translator's editor can autocomplete and
# validate the catalog beside them — and the two tools that write them disagree
# about one thing. The compiler serializes with `JSON.stringify(…, 2)`, which
# puts every array element on its own line; oxfmt collapses a short array onto
# one. A schema whose `required` list holds a single string lands on whichever
# side of oxfmt's width the string happens to fall, so `vp fmt` and the next
# build take turns rewriting the same file and `vp fmt --check` fails on
# generated output nobody touched.
#
# The catalogs themselves stay formatted: they are plain objects with no arrays
# to collapse, they have no such conflict, and people do edit them.
**/zintl/.schemas/
